An async WebSocket client against Deriv's documented API
(https://developers.deriv.com/docs/). Deriv multiplexes ordinary
request/response traffic and subscription push messages (ticks) on a
single connection, correlated by a caller-assigned req_id — this
implementation runs one background reader task (_read_loop) that
demultiplexes incoming messages to either a pending request's
asyncio.Future (by req_id) or a live subscription's asyncio.Queue (by
symbol), so a request/response call and an active tick subscription
never race to read the same connection.

submit_order maps the broker-agnostic OrderRequest onto Deriv's
Multipliers contract type (MULTUP/MULTDOWN) — the closest Deriv
product to a directional position with stop-loss/take-profit.

IMPORTANT: written against Deriv's documented request/response shapes
but NOT integration-tested against a live/demo Deriv account — this
sandbox has no network access to wss://ws.derivws.com. Tests exercise
DerivGateway's own logic (request correlation, error mapping, DTO
construction) against a scripted fake connection. Flagged prominently
in the module docstring and docs/roadmap.md's technical debt section
— particularly the fixed 'multiplier' value in submit_order and the
approximated BUY/SELL inference in get_trade_history, both of which
need confirming against a real account before production use.

11 tests covering construction, connect/authorize (success and
failure), account info, candles, order submission (filled and
rejected), and position mapping.
